.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt KLDINFO 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldinfo
.Nd display dependency and version information about kernel loadable objects
held in KLD module (.ko) file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl rv
.\".Ar
file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility parses ELF header of KLD
.Ar file Ns Pa .ko ,
then searches for available Kernel Loadable objects and shows their dependency
and version information. If path to the file is given the utility tries to
open it directly, it quits if open fails. Otherwise, it searches for
.Va file.ko
in directories set by
.Va kern.module_path
sysctl variable.
The
.Pa .ko
extension name is not mandatory, it will be added while searching for the
.Va file .
It does not hurt to specify it though.
.Pp
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl r
Extract version information of found objects. Otherwise print only dependencies.
.It Fl v
Be more verbose when parsing ELF.
.El 
.Sh NOTES
The kernel file
.Va /boot/kernel/kernel
can also be used as parameter. In this case
.Nm
will show all modules builtin into the kernel along with their corresponding
information. Note, the output can be very excessive.
.El 
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /boot/kernel -compact
.It Pa /boot/kernel
default directory containing loadable modules.
Modules must have an extension of
.Pa .ko .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
To show info about module by module name:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\*[Gt] kldinfo foo
.Ed
.Pp
To show info about module by file name within the module path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\*[Gt] kldinfo foo.ko
.Ed
.Pp
To show info about module by relative path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\*[Gt] kldinfo ./foo.ko
.Ed
.Pp
Or by full path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\*[Gt] kldinfo /boot/kernel/foo.ko
.Ed
.Pp
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload 8 ,
.Xr kldstat 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
